{
    "map": {
        "description": "Creates a raster layer from a multidimensional raster dataset or a multidimensional raster layer by slicing data along defined variables and dimensions.",
        "dimension.descr": "<xdoc><p>The dimension along which the variables will be sliced. This parameter is required when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Dimension Definition</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">By Iteration</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "dimension.title": "Dimension",
        "dimension_def.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the method that will be used to slice the dimension.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ALL\">All</span>—The full range for each dimension will be used. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"BY_RANGES\">By Ranges</span>—The dimension will be sliced using a range or a list of ranges.</li><li><span title=\"BY_ITERATION\">By Iteration</span>—The dimension will be sliced over a specified interval size.</li><li><span title=\"BY_VALUE\">By Values</span>—The dimension will be sliced using a list of dimension values.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "dimension_def.domain.ALL": "All",
        "dimension_def.domain.BY_ITERATION": "By Iteration",
        "dimension_def.domain.BY_RANGES": "By Ranges",
        "dimension_def.domain.BY_VALUE": "By Values",
        "dimension_def.title": "Dimension Definition",
        "dimension_ranges.descr": "<xdoc><p>The range or list of ranges for the specified dimension.</p><p>The data will be sliced based on the dimension name and the minimum and maximum values for the range. This parameter is required when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Dimension Definition</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">By Ranges</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "dimension_ranges.dt.title1": "Dimension",
        "dimension_ranges.dt.title2": "Minimum Value",
        "dimension_ranges.dt.title3": "Maximum Value",
        "dimension_ranges.title": "Range",
        "dimension_values.descr": "<xdoc><p>A list of values for the specified dimension. This parameter is required when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Dimension Definition</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">By Values</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "dimension_values.dt.title1": "Dimension",
        "dimension_values.dt.title2": "Values",
        "dimension_values.title": "Values",
        "dimensionless.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the layer will have dimension values. This parameter is only active if a single slice is selected to create a layer.<ul><li>Checked—The layer will not have dimension values.</li><li>Unchecked—The layer will have dimension values. This is the default.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "dimensionless.title": "Dimensionless",
        "end_of_first_iteration.descr": "<xdoc><p>The end of the first interval. This interval will be used to iterate through the dataset. This parameter is required when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Dimension Definition</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">By Iteration</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "end_of_first_iteration.title": "End of first iteration",
        "in_multidimensional_raster.descr": "<xdoc><p>The input multidimensional raster dataset.</p><p>Supported inputs are netCDF, GRIB, HDF, CRF, and Zarr files, a multidimensional mosaic dataset, a multidimensional image service, an OPeNDAP URL, or a multidimensional raster layer.<note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">A Zarr file must have an extension of .zarr and a .zgroup file in the folder.</p></p></xdoc>",
        "in_multidimensional_raster.title": "Input Multidimensional Raster",
        "iteration_step.descr": "<xdoc><p>The frequency with which the data will be sliced. This parameter is required when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Dimension Definition</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">By Iteration</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "iteration_step.title": "Step",
        "iteration_unit.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the iteration unit that will be used. This parameter is required when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Dimension Definition</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">By Iteration</span> and the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Dimension</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">StdTime</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "iteration_unit.domain.DAYS": "Days",
        "iteration_unit.domain.HOURS": "Hours",
        "iteration_unit.domain.MONTHS": "Months",
        "iteration_unit.domain.WEEKS": "Weeks",
        "iteration_unit.domain.YEARS": "Years",
        "iteration_unit.title": "Unit",
        "out_multidimensional_raster_layer.descr": "The output multidimensional raster layer.",
        "out_multidimensional_raster_layer.title": "Output Multidimensional Raster Layer",
        "params.category1": "Interpolate irregular data",
        "spatial_reference.descr": "<xdoc><p>The coordinate system for the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Output Multidimensional Raster Layer</span> parameter value. This parameter only applies when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Multidimensional Raster</span> parameter value is in Zarr format. Use this parameter to define the spatial reference if it is missing in the data.</p></xdoc>",
        "spatial_reference.title": "Spatial Reference",
        "start_of_first_iteration.descr": "<xdoc><p>The beginning of the first interval. This interval will be used to iterate through the dataset. This parameter is required when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Dimension Definition</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">By Iteration</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "start_of_first_iteration.title": "Start of first iteration",
        "template.descr": "<xdoc><p>The extent (bounding box) of the layer. Choose the appropriate <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Extent</span> option for the layer.</p><ul><li>Current Display Extent—The extent will be based on the active map or scene.</li><li>Draw Extent—The extent will be based on a rectangle drawn on the map or scene.</li><li>Extent of a Layer—The extent will be based on an active map layer. Choose an available layer or use the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Extent of data in all layers</span> option. Each map layer has the following options:<p><ul><li>All Features—The extent of all features.</li><li>Selected Features —The extent of the selected features.</li><li>Visible Features—The extent of visible features.</li></ul></p></li><li>Browse—The extent will be based on a dataset.</li><li>Clipboard—The extent can be copied to and from the clipboard.<ul><li>Copy Extent—Copies the extent and coordinate system to the clipboard.</li><li>Paste Extent—Pastes the extent and coordinate system from the clipboard. If the clipboard does not include a coordinate system, the extent will use the map’s coordinate system.</li></ul></li><li>Reset Extent—The extent will be reset to the default value.</li></ul><p>When coordinates are manually provided, the coordinates must be numeric values and in the active map&apos;s coordinate system. The map may use different display units than the provided coordinates. Use a negative value sign for south and west coordinates.</p></xdoc>",
        "template.title": "Extent",
        "title": "Make Multidimensional Raster Layer",
        "variables.descr": "The variables that will be included in the output multidimensional raster layer. If no variable is specified, the first variable will be used.",
        "variables.title": "Variables"
    }
}
